# Site POV (isaque.it /portifolio)

## Core message

- Motto: **Complexity, simplified.**
- Philosophy: **Simple isn't easy. That's why I love to build it.**
- Hero identity: name **Isaque Costa** is the primary headline; motto is the tagline under it.
- Location on the site: **Dublin / Ireland** (do not change without explicit request).

## Structure of meaning

| Surface | Role |
|---------|------|
| Hero | Who + credibility signals (stats, languages, CTA) |
| Journey | Surface of *what shaped the work* + how I think — five era beats, not a CV |
| Stories | Three oversized case teasers linking to dedicated pages |
| Selected projects | Catalog grid of career work; visual identity per era (do not redesign lightly) |
| Contact | Clear paths to talk |

Deep narrative (problem → difficulty → simplification → change + chapters) lives on **dedicated case pages** (`cases/{cube,miodelivery,platform}/`), not inline on the homepage.

## Featured vs catalog

- **Case studies** (`data/projects.json`) = narrative only (`cube`, `miodelivery`, `platform`) at `cases/{id}/`. Homepage teasers stay shallow; pages stay deep and layout-personal.
- **Selected projects** (`data/catalog.json`) = browsable archive. Card opens a detail modal (`#project-{id}`) unless `caseId` is set — then navigate to `cases/{caseId}/`.
- Never mark the whole catalog as “featured” the way `_legacy` did.

## Brand and visual language

- Brand signal: the cube (hero photo cube + Rubik solver on the cube case page).
- Palette: CSS variables in `assets/css/tokens.css` (`--cube-yellow`, `--cube-red`, `--cube-blue`, `--cube-green`, `--cube-orange`, `--cube-coral`).
- Type: Newsreader (display) + Instrument Sans (UI). EN/PT via `data/copy.json` and bilingual fields in JSON data.
- Era accent colors (catalog / journey wash): design `#F5617F`, hardware `#FFD22B`, ideyou `#FF5356`, teaching `#9900CC`, platform `#0076F3`.
- IdeYou-style section color wash on Journey + Stories hover/focus (whole band repaints to the accent).

## Do not

- Turn the hero into a dashboard of pills, badges, or stats-on-cube faces.
- Default to generic AI aesthetics (purple gradients, cream+terracotta broadsheet, glow pills).
- Flatten Journey into a list of job titles.
- Reintroduce runtime machine-translation (legacy MyMemory); keep authored EN/PT.
- Invent employers, dates, or locations that contradict `career-context.mdc`.
- Stuff full case chapters back onto the homepage.
